# Commit finished work — ask when mixed

**Incident this prevents:** an agent stashed the admin reskin to land an unrelated Mimundo commit, promised to restore it, and never did. Implementation sat uncommitted until the user noticed.

## When a task is done

- **Commit** spec + plan + implementation (and tests/migrations) in the same commit. Do **not** leave it staged “until they ask.”
- **Push / deploy** only if the user asked (`subí`, `push`, `deploy`) or you asked and they said yes.

## Never without asking and waiting for an answer

- `git stash` (any form, including `--include-untracked` / `--keep-index`)
- `git restore` / discard / clean of files the user or another session owns
- Setting aside “unrelated” WIP so a hook can pass
- Bundling two features into one commit, or dropping one of them, without asking

If the tree already has other staged or unstaged work that is **not** this task, stop:

> Hay otro WIP en el árbol (`<files>`). ¿Lo meto en este commit, lo dejo intacto, o commiteamos por separado?

Do not stash, restore, or commit that WIP until they answer.

## End of turn

If product files are still modified or staged: **commit them or ask**. Do not end a turn with silent staged WIP.

## Still ask (do not decide alone)

- `SKIP_E2E=1`
- Tests failing at the commit gate — **`990-tests-failure-confirmation.mdc`**
- Push/deploy if they did not ask

Superpowers “commit the spec now” **loses** to this rule and to **`29-spec-driven-development.mdc`** (spec-only drafts stay uncommitted until implementation is ready; then commit together).
